  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ain Shohayota (Legal Aid)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Bangladesh):  .Bangladesh suffers from a dysfunctional rule of law system, which negatively impacts progress toward achieving its democracy, development, and good governance goals. Formal justice institutions are complex and fraught with delays, leading to low levels of citizen confidence and trust in the judiciary. Marginalized communities, in particular, face inadequate access to justice. USAID&apos;s Ain Shohayota (Legal Aid) activity will improve citizens&apos; access to justice, strengthen the judicial system, and enhance services for the poor and vulnerable populations. This activity will promote people-centered justice through increased public participation, inclusivity, and data-driven approaches to strengthen the justice system...With FY 2024 funds, Ain Shohayota will increase demand for responsive justice services, promote pro bono legal assistance, and build and utilize an evidence base to enhance justice services. The activity will collaborate with government ministries and the judiciary on effective case management and court administration systems are in place. This initiative will strengthen alternative dispute resolution mechanisms, such as mediation, at the local level. This activity will partner with local civil society organizations to promote people-centered justice by raising awareness of human rights and legal aid services, particularly among vulnerable youth. To fill a gap in legal education, the activity will encourage law students to understand and provide legal aid and pro bono legal services through an internship program with six universities..This IM contributes to the Women, Peace and Security earmark ($100k), Private Sector Engagement ($100k)k and Youth in Development ($100k) issues. The activity is in line with the Integrated Country Strategy Mission Objective 2.2 - Citizen confidence in governance institutions increases and USAID&apos;s CDCS Mission Development Objective 1 - Democracy strengthened for an inclusive society.</narrative>
  </description>
